{{define "title"}}Your password was changed{{end}}
{{define "content"}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Hello{{if .Name}} {{.Name}}{{end}},</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">The password on your Chronos account was {{if .ViaReset}}reset{{else}}changed{{end}} on
  <strong>{{datetime .OccurredAt}}</strong>{{if .Location}} from {{.Location}}{{end}}{{if .Device}}, using {{.Device}}{{end}}.</p>
{{if .ViaReset}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">It was changed through a reset link rather than by someone who knew the old
  password, and every session on the account has been signed out.</p>
{{end}}
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">If this was you, nothing further is needed.</p>
<!--
  The "this wasn't me" link triggers a protective action and NEVER authenticates
  the person clicking it (NOTIFICATIONS §4). A leaked alert email therefore
  cannot become an account takeover. Absent it, the message sends the reader to
  a page that makes them sign in, which is the safe degradation.
-->
{{if .RevokeURL}}
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
  <a href="{{.RevokeURL}}" style="display:inline-block;background:#b42318;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;">This wasn't me</a>
</p>
<p style="margin:0;color:#6b7280;font-size:13px;">This signs out every session and requires a new password. It does not sign you in.</p>
{{else}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">If it wasn't, somebody else has control of this account.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
  <a href="{{url "/settings/security"}}" style="display:inline-block;background:#b42318;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;">Change the password again</a>
</p>
{{end}}
{{end}}
